# User Rules - Global Development Preferences

## Communication Style
- Provide concise, actionable responses with specific code examples
- Prioritize practical implementation over theoretical explanations
- Use bullet points and clear headings for complex instructions
- Include relevant file paths and component names when suggesting changes

## Code Quality Standards
- Always use TypeScript for new files with strict type checking
- Prefer functional components with React hooks and modern patterns
- Write self-documenting code with clear variable and function names
- Include JSDoc comments for complex functions and components
- Follow the existing project's code style and patterns exactly
- Use CSS modules with BEM-style class names instead of inline styles

## Development Workflow - V0.app FIRST (Vercel Integration)
- **PRIORITY**: ALWAYS use V0.app first for component generation before manual coding
